  "multipleInstance": true,
  "text": "<p>18 problems drawn at random from the whole Midterm 2 pool — about twice a real Midterm 2 — with fresh random numbers and a different selection of problems every time you start a new instance. 4 hours, the real exam's pace (about 13 minutes a problem). Each problem has three attempts worth 10, 7 and 4 points. Work on paper first, with one handwritten sheet and no calculator, as on the real exam; the worked solutions are visible once you finish.</p><p>Fall 2026 scope (Wed Nov 4, 7–9 pm): Lectures 13–23, HW5–9 — the DTFT, frequency response, magnitude and phase, sampling and reconstruction, A/D → filter → D/A, the DFT and its properties, spectral analysis and windows. Computing a circular convolution and the FFT are not on it, so they are not in this mock. Every problem in the pool, untimed: Mock Midterm 2 (untimed, every question).</p>",
